<title>SWEDEN: Volvo W.Europe car sales up 23.8 pct Oct.</title>
<headline>Volvo W.Europe car sales up 23.8 pct Oct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>AB Volvo Car sales in western Europe rose by 23.8 percent in October to 22,821 cars, the Association des Constructeurs Europeens d'Automobile (ACEA) said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>This lifted the Swedish vehicle maker's share of the western European market to 2.1 percent from 2.0 percent in October 1995.</p>
<p>Saab Automobile sales rose by 11.6 percent to 4,826 cars in October while Saab's market share was unchanged at 0.5 percent compared with the corresponding month a year ago.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
